# The core data of a compiler: expression trees and a symbol table.
#
# A tree lives in one list of nodes. A node refers to its operands by their
# position in that list, a `NodeId`, never by holding them (D-60): a type may
# not contain itself, by value or inside a collection. A `NodeId` has no
# literal; it comes only from `Nodes.appendIndexed`, and reading a node at a
# position the list does not have is an error, never a stray read.
#
# Names live in a symbol table, a map from `String` to `Int64` (D-61). The map
# copies each new name into its own region, and a `forEach` over the map reads
# the names in the order they were first defined (D-62).

expressions is module
expressions purpose "Build expression trees as node lists, keep names in a symbol table, and evaluate trees by recursion"
expressions path expressions
expressions imports standard.list
expressions imports standard.map
expressions imports standard.math
expressions imports standard.string
expressions imports standard.test
expressions exports Operands
expressions exports Expr
expressions exports Nodes
expressions exports NodeId
expressions exports Symbols
expressions exports EvalError
expressions exports addNumber
expressions exports addName
expressions exports addSum
expressions exports addProduct
expressions exports evaluate
expressions exports countNumbers
expressions exports joinNames

Operands is record
Operands purpose "The two operands of a sum or product node, by their positions in the node list"
Operands typeParameter none
Operands field left NodeId
Operands field right NodeId

Expr is enum
Expr purpose "One node of an expression tree: a number, a name, or the sum or product of two other nodes"
Expr typeParameter none
Expr variant number Int64
Expr variant name String
Expr variant sum Operands
Expr variant product Operands

Nodes is typeInstance
Nodes purpose "The nodes of one or more expression trees, in the order they were added"
Nodes in none
Nodes instantiates list.List Expr

NodeId is alias
NodeId purpose "The position of a node in a Nodes list, received when the node is added"
NodeId typeParameter none
NodeId aliasOf Int64
NodeId indexes Nodes

Symbols is typeInstance
Symbols purpose "The value of each defined name, in the order the names were first defined"
Symbols in none
Symbols instantiates map.Map String Int64

EvalError is enum
EvalError purpose "Why an expression could not be evaluated, with what the caller needs to report it"
EvalError typeParameter none
EvalError variant unknownName none
EvalError variant missingNode Int64

