# ---------------------------------------------------------------- evaluating a tree

evaluate is operation
evaluate purpose "Evaluate the tree whose root is at a position, operands first, by recursion"
evaluate invariant numberIsItself "A number node evaluates to its number"
evaluate invariant nameFromSymbols "A name node evaluates to the name's value in the symbol table"
evaluate invariant operandsFirst "A sum or product node evaluates to the sum or product of its operands' values"
evaluate invariant rejectsUnknownName "A name with no value in the symbol table is an unknownName error"
evaluate invariant rejectsMissingNode "A position the node list does not have is a missingNode error carrying the position"
evaluate typeParameter none
evaluate input nodes Nodes borrowed
evaluate input symbols Symbols borrowed
evaluate input at NodeId copied
evaluate output Int64
evaluate outputOwnedBy none
evaluate raises EvalError
evaluate effect none
evaluate uses none
evaluate memoryHeap false
evaluate async false
evaluate maxRecursion 64
evaluate label begin loopKind none
evaluate label begin within none
evaluate label missing loopKind none
evaluate label missing within none
evaluate label reportMissing loopKind none
evaluate label reportMissing within none
evaluate label inspect loopKind none
evaluate label inspect within none
evaluate label isNumber loopKind none
evaluate label isNumber within none
evaluate label isName loopKind none
evaluate label isName within none
evaluate label found loopKind none
evaluate label found within none
evaluate label unknown loopKind none
evaluate label unknown within none
evaluate label isSum loopKind none
evaluate label isSum within none
evaluate label sumSecond loopKind none
evaluate label sumSecond within none
evaluate label sumBoth loopKind none
evaluate label sumBoth within none
evaluate label isProduct loopKind none
evaluate label isProduct within none
evaluate label productSecond loopKind none
evaluate label productSecond within none
evaluate label productBoth loopKind none
evaluate label productBoth within none
evaluate label passSumLeft loopKind none
evaluate label passSumLeft within none
evaluate label passSumRight loopKind none
evaluate label passSumRight within none
evaluate label passProductLeft loopKind none
evaluate label passProductLeft within none
evaluate label passProductRight loopKind none
evaluate label passProductRight within none
evaluate let none
evaluate at begin do readNode
evaluate at begin branch ifError readNode goto missing else goto inspect
evaluate at missing match readError list.IndexOutOfRange
evaluate at missing case list.IndexOutOfRange.outOfRange bind badPosition Int64 goto reportMissing
evaluate at reportMissing do makeMissing
evaluate at reportMissing return error missingError
evaluate at inspect match node Expr
evaluate at inspect case Expr.number bind number Int64 goto isNumber
evaluate at inspect case Expr.name bind text String goto isName
evaluate at inspect case Expr.sum bind sumOperands Operands goto isSum
evaluate at inspect case Expr.product bind productOperands Operands goto isProduct
evaluate at isNumber return ok number
evaluate at isName do lookUp
evaluate at isName branch ifError lookUp goto unknown else goto found
evaluate at found return ok named
evaluate at unknown do makeUnknown
evaluate at unknown return error unknownError
evaluate at isSum do sumLeftId
evaluate at isSum do sumLeft
evaluate at isSum branch ifError sumLeft goto passSumLeft else goto sumSecond
evaluate at sumSecond do sumRightId
evaluate at sumSecond do sumRight
evaluate at sumSecond branch ifError sumRight goto passSumRight else goto sumBoth
evaluate at sumBoth do addBoth
evaluate at sumBoth return ok total
evaluate at isProduct do productLeftId
evaluate at isProduct do productLeft
evaluate at isProduct branch ifError productLeft goto passProductLeft else goto productSecond
evaluate at productSecond do productRightId
evaluate at productSecond do productRight
evaluate at productSecond branch ifError productRight goto passProductRight else goto productBoth
evaluate at productBoth do multiplyBoth
evaluate at productBoth return ok product
evaluate at passSumLeft return error sumLeftError
evaluate at passSumRight return error sumRightError
evaluate at passProductLeft return error productLeftError
evaluate at passProductRight return error productRightError

